# DementiaSupport — Cursor Rules

## Final stack (locked)

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Mobile | **Flutter** (patient + caregiver) |
| Mobile DB | **Drift → SQLite** (offline source of truth) |
| Voice hot path | **Sherpa ONNX** via `VoiceEngine` (on-device; never blocked by cloud) |
| Web SaaS | **Next.js** on **Vercel** |
| Backend | **Supabase** (Auth, Postgres+RLS, Storage, Realtime) — required |
| Cloud brain | **Google Gemini** cold path only (online enhancement) |
| Sync | Local write + outbox → Supabase when online |

**Not in voice loop:** Vercel, Supabase Realtime, Google APIs.

**Legacy:** Capacitor `app/` and Expo `mobile/` are reference only until Flutter owns sessions. Prefer new work under `apps/flutter` + `apps/web` + `supabase/`.

## Product

- Offline-first cognitive engagement; optional supervisor/caregiver.
- Not a medical device: no diagnostic claims.

## Agent build / secrets

- User may provide Vercel / Supabase / Google tokens for CLI deploy (`vercel`, `supabase`, `flutter`).
- Store only in `.env.local` / CI secrets — **never commit** PATs or service keys.
- Prefer agent-driven scaffold, migrate, deploy over manual steps.

## UI edits

- Flutter: `lib/theme/`, `lib/widgets/`, feature screens under `lib/features/`.
- Web: Next.js `app/` routes + shared components.
- Domain logic (session engine, fuzzy match, scoring) in shared package — survives redesigns.

## UX

- Patient: voice-first, huge targets, chip fallback if STT fails.
- Caregiver web: memories, trends, flags. Mobile caregiver: light setup + uploads.
